    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Let’s name the functions that relate the dog’s distance from the post and the time since its owner left: function \(f\) for Day 1, function \(g\) for Day 2, function \(h\) for Day 3. The input of each function is time in seconds, \(t\).</para>
        <para id="para-00002">Day 1(<media alt="Nonlinear function. time in seconds and distance from post in feet."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_05_03_01.svg"/></media>)</para>
        <para id="para-00003">Day 2(<media alt="Nonlinear function. time in seconds and distance from post in feet."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_05_03_02.svg"/></media>)</para>
        <para id="para-00004">Day 3(<media alt="Nonlinear function. time in seconds and distance from post in feet."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_05_03_03.svg"/></media>)</para>
      
      <para id="para-00005">Use <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00001">function notation</term> to complete the table.</para>
